Byte-identical reproduction patches for the AD5M Pro stock kernel build

Applies on top of `iLotusK9/linux_kernel_aw_t113@5.4.61` (commit 349a0b9).

What this patch does:

 1. Wires up CONFIG_CAN_SUN8I (Kconfig + Makefile) so the orphan
    drivers/net/can/sunxi_can.c + sunxi_can_asm.S in the BSP source
    actually build. Original wiring lived in the (NDA-only)
    Allwinner T113-Linux-Auto-v1.1 SDK overlay; this patch reproduces
    it from the canonical Allwinner Tina pattern.

 2. Adds a reconstructed drivers/net/can/sunxi_can_asm.h with 30
    SUNXI_* register/bit-mask defines (derived from mainline
    drivers/net/can/sun4i_can.c — same Allwinner CAN IP) and 12
    can_asm_* function prototypes inferred from call-site analysis of
    sunxi_can.c. The original header was closed-source from the
    T113-Linux-Auto SDK; the public BSP omits it, leaving sunxi_can.c
    uncompilable. See in-file commentary for the reconstruction method.

 3. Adds a stub drivers/staging/rtl8821cu/Kconfig (sourced from
    drivers/staging/Kconfig right after rtl8188eu) so the captured stock
    .config's `CONFIG_RTL8821CU=m` line resolves at the correct IKCONFIG
    position. No corresponding Makefile target exists, so the symbol is
    config-only — no module is produced.

 4. Hides 14 newer Kconfig entries that exist in the iLotusK9 BSP
    snapshot but did NOT exist in the source FF built from (the
    T113-Linux-Auto-v1.1 SDK shipped an older BSP). Without this, the
    embedded IKCONFIG.gz contains 14 extra "# CONFIG_X is not set" lines
    that don't appear in stock's IKCONFIG. The hidden entries are:
      BT_HCIUART_RTL3WIRE       (drivers/bluetooth/Kconfig)
      RTL8189FS                 (drivers/net/wireless/rtl8189fs/Kconfig)
      PINCTRL_SUN55IW3 + _R     (drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/Kconfig)
      MFD_ACX00                 (drivers/mfd/Kconfig)
      SND_SOC_SUNXI_SPDIF/DMIC/DAUDIO/COMPONENTS + the menu header
                                (sound/soc/sunxi_v2/Kconfig)
      SND_SOC_TD100             (sound/soc/codecs/Kconfig)
      RPMSG_SUNXI_TTY + _CLIENT_SAMPLE
                                (drivers/rpmsg/Kconfig)
    Each is gated behind `depends on FORCE_HIDE_NEWER_BSP`, an undefined
    Kconfig symbol that Kconfig evaluates as `n`, so the stanzas are
    invisible to olddefconfig.

 5. Forces CONFIG_PLUGIN_HOSTCC to "" so CONFIG_GCC_PLUGINS auto-vanishes
    (it has `depends on PLUGIN_HOSTCC != ""`). Stock's build host had no
    g++ on PATH, so PLUGIN_HOSTCC was detected empty by Kconfig's
    $(shell,...) probe. Our build host DOES have g++ + plugin headers,
    so Kconfig would normally fill in "g++" and enable the plugin
    subsystem — leaking plugin-emitted code into the Image and diverging
    from stock. Patch overrides the auto-detect to a hardcoded "".

Generated for: tools/build/build-bsp-kernel-stock.sh
Reference doc: docs/research/2026-06-04-byte-identical-kernel-reproduction.md

