(`pwm-sunxi-g_dev.c`) from ayueying/linux-5.4 @ 2022-09-08 snapshot.
Source: https://github.com/ayueying/linux-5.4/blob/master/drivers/pwm/pwm-sunxi-g_dev.c
sha256: f53450ae744d2507440e0d6dc000e630e68d807746c04c41573901e6f547ff05 (5668 bytes)
Copyright (C) 2019 AllWinner.

Stock's symbol-set diff (kallsyms-decoded) showed 9 missing PWM-related
symbols (sunxi_pwm_class/dev/exit/fops/init/open/release/unlocked_ioctl +
__initcall_sunxi_pwm_init6) — all defined in this single file. The iLotusK9
BSP submodule we pinned (349a0b9) had dropped this source between FF's
build snapshot and ours, while keeping the same CONFIG_PWM_SUNXI_GROUP=y
knob. Stock's Makefile compiled both pwm-sunxi-group.o AND pwm-sunxi-g_dev.o
from the same config; iLotusK9 only compiles the former.

See outputs/kallsyms-symbol-diff.md for the full classification.

